 "_meta": {
  "title": "Silicon Valley Clean Energy (SVCE) generation rates vs PG&E bundled generation, by PG&E rate plan",
  "retrieved": "2026-10-24",
  "units": "USD per kWh",
  "kind": "observed (rate sheet columns) + inferred (adjustment and totals)",
  "effective": "2026-01-01",
  "how_to_use": "SVCE customer all-in $/kWh = PG&E bundled total rate (tariffs_pge.json) + greenstart_adjustment_usd_per_kwh (or greenprime_adjustment_usd_per_kwh) for the same plan/season/period. The adjustment = SVCE 'Generation Service' (SVCE generation + PG&E PCIA + franchise fee) - PG&E 'Generation Service' (PG&E generation + bundled PCIA). PG&E delivery charges, the Base Services Charge and baseline credit are the same for both.",
  "notes": [
   "SVCE rate sheet footnotes: '1 SVCE Generation Rates, without added PG&E fees, effective 1/1/2026'; '2 SVCE Generation Service reflects our price for Generation, with added PG&E fees (PCIA and Franchise Fees), effective 1/1/2026. SVCE sets its rates based on the 2017 PCIA vintage, which is the most common vintage for our customers ... the all-in discount or premium varies because PG&E applies different fees by vintage.'; '3 PG&E Generation service rate effective 1/1/2026'.",
   "GreenPrime: '+$0.00740 Same as applicable rate, with 0.0074/kWh adder for 100% Renewable energy'.",
   "Check: the PG&E 'Generation Service' column equals PG&E Sheet 3 generation (Mar 1, 2026) minus the $0.01011 bundled PCIA (e.g. E-TOU-C summer peak 0.20782 - 0.01011 = 0.19771). PG&E's June 1, 2026 total-rate update (D.26-04-036) is not reflected in SVCE's sheet; if that update changed PG&E generation, the adjustment is off by that change (UNCONFIRMED).",
   "PG&E 2017-vintage PCIA in current schedules is $0.03661/kWh (effective March 1, 2026, E-TOU-C/E-ELEC PCIA vintage table), vs the $0.03720 PCIA + franchise fee SVCE used on 1/1/2026.",
   "Totals are rounded to 5 decimals."
  ],
